{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books","id":1504254,"title":"Best M20 books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-03T05:51:33-08:00","id":1504254,"title":"Best M20 books?","content":"What do you find are the best books to use/get in M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T06:06:28-08:00","id":1504257,"title":"","content":"\u2026all of them? Well, almost. <br /> <br /> M20 is definitely the first to get, of course. <b>Book of Secrets</b> and <b>Gods &amp; Monsters</b> are basically \u201cstuff we wanted to put in M20, but didn't have space for\u201d, with the former giving additional traits and rules while the latter provides what amounts to a bestiary (including rules for making them as playable characters).<br /> <br /> <b>How Do You Do That?</b> gets a lot of flack; but I would argue that most of that flack comes from veterans of previous editions who are already familiar with what the Magick system is capable of, and who question some of the choices that this book made. But most of the book is solid, and is essentially part three of \u201cstuff that we couldn't fit in the core book. In a similar vein, <b>The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> breaks the Syndicate's monopoly on money magick, and shows just what it's capable of. <br /> <br /> The <b>Mage Cookbook</b> can be skipped, unless you're into cooking. It's literally what it says it is: a cookbook. And <b>Victorian Mage</b> can probably be skipped if you plan on focusing on the 21st century. <br /> <br /> <b>Book of the Fallen</b>, <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, and the upcoming <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> are the faction books. <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> has a supplement, <b>The Operative's Handbook</b>; and <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> will be getting <i>two</i> supplements, one dealing with signature characters (I think) and the other dealing with the Disparate factions. <br /> <br /> And then there's <b>M20 Sorcerer</b>; though there's a Storyteller's Vault product (<b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b>) that it was based on, and that I would suggest that you take a serious look at. <br /> <hr /><br /> And speaking of Storyteller's Vault, there are quite a few products from there that I'd recommend. <b>Mage Made Easy</b> and <b>Fallen Companions: Among the Masses</b> were written by Satyros Phil Brucato; the former essentially outlines what he wanted M20 to be if it hadn't been designed as a celebration of the previous editions; and the latter is basically a supplement for <b>Book of the Fallen</b> and <b>Gods &amp; Monsters</b>, dealing with Sleepers who get roped into the Nephandic world. Charles Seigel is another prolific STV contributor who provides high quality content, including the aforementioned <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b>; but also <b>Enlightened Grimoire</b>, <b>Mystic Armory</b>, and <b>Sources of Power</b>, which are compendia of rotes, Wonders, and Nodes, respectively. He also published <b>Paradigms Explored: Number and Shape</b>, the second in a (so far) three-book series offering worked examples of magical paradigms, and by far my personal favorite. But then, <b>Number and Shape</b> speaks to me personally; your mileage may vary. The others in that series are <b>Wyrd and Weft</b>, which tackles Nordic Magick, and <b>Fairy Faith</b>, which doubles as a crossover book with <b>Changeling</b>. <br /> <br /> The STV <b>Book of Fragments</b> deals with Minor Spheres; and <b>Foreign Magick</b> leverages that to crossover play, with Minor Spheres based on <b>Vampire</b>, <b>Werewolf</b>, <b>Wraith</b>, and <b>Changeling</b>. <br /> <br /> Finally, I would recommend <b>Ascension's Landscape</b> and <b>Strange Yesterdays</b> as a pair of books addressing questions that Storytellers really ought to consider; and <b>Never-Real Worlds</b> is a sourcebook dealing with Paradox Realms. <i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-03-2023, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T08:10:39-08:00","id":1504264,"title":"","content":"Rich Bastards Guide to Magic would be my recommendation for the best, being the most unique and fun addition of the 20th Edition.<br /> <br /> The worst, on the other hand, Gods&amp;Monsters. The OG Bygone Bestiary is way better and contains way more sought out creatures and beings.<br /> <br /> As for the most mediocre, M20 Sorcerer in my opinion. Just Revised Sorcerer but slightly different and a bit worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T08:24:15-08:00","id":1504265,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for your perspectives! Dataweaver, I appreciate your mentioning the STV books. Hadn't thought about asking about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T16:42:40-08:00","id":1504297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books#post1504254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you find are the best books to use/get in M20?</div> </div> </div> </div>The newest Technocracy's Convention books are excellent, good, interesting, and it is definitely positive and worthwhile to carefully browse and read through these M:tA supplements, in order to gain a better understanding of Enlightened Scientists, their ambitions and goals, their capabilities and methods, and of course their special or particular outlooks and also important personal values.<br /> <br /> They are also excellent in the context of the World of Darkness as a role-playing game setting. Maybe they are especially relevant in the context of WoD as a rather radical and complex setting, that is also of course intricate, wonderful, understandable, and optimistic. Also it clearly has to be mentioned that WoD distincly contains and supports various interesting, nice, and succesful computer games, literature, and card games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T17:03:27-08:00","id":1504300,"title":"","content":"The only catch is that they're written for MRev, not M20. But with that in mind, I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T00:57:19-08:00","id":1504821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books?p=1504300#post1504300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only catch is that they're written for MRev, not M20. But with that in mind, I agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this, I felt that I was missing some important technical detail in regard to these M:tA books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T05:52:41-08:00","id":1504837,"title":"","content":"They occupy a weird place in the World of Darkness publication history: the first of them, Iteration X, was one of the last books published for the original World of Darkness back in 2003, just before the whole thing was shut down and White Wolf switched over to what's now called the Chronicles of Darkness. The other four were published about a year before Brucato started work on M20, as part of the revival of the original World of Darkness that was well underway at the time: the time: while they're technically written for MRev, they're <i>set </i>\u201cten years after the apocalyptic events that threatened to end the world, but didn't quite\u201d. As such, they also provide information on how to adjust the MRev setting to run in the early 2010s. <br /> <br /> So while they're technically MRev and not M20, the bulk of them were written in a way that's\u2026 more like M20 than MRev. But not quite, because M20 hadn't been written yet when they came out. So that's why, for instance, the <b>Syndicate Convention Book </b>doesn't talk about Focus being composed of Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments, but instead talks about how the Syndicate's paradigm of Hypereconomics features Infrastructures, Personnel, Expertise, and Money as foci. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, M20 incorporated elements from the Convention Books: they're the reason why M20 has the Technocratic Sphere variants of Data and Primal Utility, and why Dimensional Science is more elaborate than how it was presented in the original <b>Void Engineers</b> book back in the late 90s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T21:13:14-07:00","id":1505526,"title":"","content":"There is a bit more fluff for M20. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/220431/M20-The-Art-of-Mage-20-Years-and-More?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Art of Mage - 20 Years and More</b></a> is a collection of art and comments about how various artists have interpreted Mage in previous books of the line. OK, if you are into it. It isn\u00a8t the first being published. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/374544/M20-Welcome-to-the-Rock-A-Jumpstart-for-Mages-Technocracy-Reloaded?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Technocracy Reloaded Jumpstart</b></a> contains an adventure <i>Welcome to the Rock</i>, which I say does a sufficient job to introduce new players to the game. Which cannot be said about <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/131409/Mage-The-Ascension-20th-Anniversary-Edition-Quickstart?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Mage: The Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition Quickstart</b></a> and the setting of <i>Toll for the Trolls</i>, as it concentrates on the gutter magic that might not be up to most new players expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-23-2023, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T06:23:19-07:00","id":1506135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books?p=1504837#post1504837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They occupy a weird place in the World of Darkness publication history: the first of them, Iteration X, was one of the last books published for the original World of Darkness back in 2003, just before the whole thing was shut down and White Wolf switched over to what's now called the Chronicles of Darkness. The other four were published about a year before Brucato started work on M20, as part of the revival of the original World of Darkness that was well underway at the time: the time: while they're technically written for MRev, they're <i>set </i>\u201cten years after the apocalyptic events that threatened to end the world, but didn't quite\u201d. As such, they also provide information on how to adjust the MRev setting to run in the early 2010s.<br /> <br /> So while they're technically MRev and not M20, the bulk of them were written in a way that's\u2026 more like M20 than MRev. But not quite, because M20 hadn't been written yet when they came out. So that's why, for instance, the <b>Syndicate Convention Book </b>doesn't talk about Focus being composed of Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments, but instead talks about how the Syndicate's paradigm of Hypereconomics features Infrastructures, Personnel, Expertise, and Money as foci.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, M20 incorporated elements from the Convention Books: they're the reason why M20 has the Technocratic Sphere variants of Data and Primal Utility, and why Dimensional Science is more elaborate than how it was presented in the original <b>Void Engineers</b> book back in the late 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any other WoD books, guides, or supplements that were likewise released distinctly just before the original World of Darkness being brought back with the 20th Anniversary Editions ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T07:18:20-07:00","id":1506139,"title":"","content":"Not that I'm aware of. The closest to it is that the Changeling relaunch included a Kithbook that, if I recall, \u201ccompleted the set\u201d as far as earlier editions we're concerned; but I think it was written with the 20th Anniversary Edition in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T04:45:01-07:00","id":1506224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books?p=1506135#post1506135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there any other WoD books, guides, or supplements that were likewise released distinctly just before the original World of Darkness being brought back with the 20th Anniversary Editions ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> The Werewolf 20th Anniversary edition had a similar publication to Changeling's <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/242685/C20-Kithbook-Boggans?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Kithbook: Boggans</a></b>, as <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/137620/W20-White-Howlers-Tribebook?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: White Howlers</a></b> completed the previous series of splats. Still, both books were written for the 20th Anniversary editions.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/125594/Dark-Ages-Darkening-Sky?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Ages: Darkening Sky</a></b> was a previously announced cross-over product for the Dark Ages lines, published in 2014. It was part of the Dark Ages line, not the Vampire: the Dark Ages 20th Anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-24-2023, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T11:19:37-07:00","id":1506325,"title":"","content":"Thus far I have added How do you do that?, Book of Secrets, and Gods and Monsters to my collection. I kickstarted Lore of the Traditions last year as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T13:40:24-07:00","id":1506527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cabaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504254-best-m20-books?p=1506224#post1506224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not for Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> The Werewolf 20th Anniversary edition had a similar publication to Changeling's <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/242685/C20-Kithbook-Boggans?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Kithbook: Boggans</a></b>, as <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/137620/W20-White-Howlers-Tribebook?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: White Howlers</a></b> completed the previous series of splats. Still, both books were written for the 20th Anniversary editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that for Werewolf RPG it would be definitely be interesting if some of the Tribal Camps (Including the radical groups, as well as the more traditional or representative organisations) were described with more attention, consideration, respect, and detail.<br /> At least two or three books or supplements could be written - for a good start - in regard to this area of the Werewolf RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}